1
00:00:05,853 --> 00:00:07,593
Listen to a car going by.

2
00:00:07,673 --> 00:00:09,917
The sound is bright and clear.

3
00:00:09,997 --> 00:00:12,430
And it is already passing as it sounds.

4
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:15,043
At no point is there a sound that stays.

5
00:00:15,878 --> 00:00:17,999
Here is a koan to hold in mind.

6
00:00:18,079 --> 00:00:20,513
This moment ceases as it arises.

7
00:00:20,593 --> 00:00:23,221
Does it arise, or does it cease?

8
00:00:24,029 --> 00:00:28,247
This video draws on The Logic,
a section of After Anatta:

9
00:00:28,417 --> 00:00:33,840
notes by John Tan, known as Thusness, on
what turned out to matter after the anatta

10
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:36,055
insight of 1997.

11
00:00:36,135 --> 00:00:40,172
Eight steps teach two logics:
the logic of substance,

12
00:00:40,252 --> 00:00:42,223
and the logic of dependency.

13
00:00:42,303 --> 00:00:44,533
But the author puts one thing first.

14
00:00:44,613 --> 00:00:49,424
The logic of dependency cannot be
understood clearly by reasoning alone.

15
00:00:49,504 --> 00:00:53,405
It needs a direct insight into
what a phenomenon actually is.

16
00:00:53,485 --> 00:00:57,431
A sound, a thought, a
cup. Seeing comes first.

17
00:00:58,246 --> 00:01:00,789
So he names four insights after anatta.

18
00:01:00,869 --> 00:01:05,204
Without seeing them clearly, and
confirming them again and again in direct

19
00:01:05,284 --> 00:01:08,587
experience, the logic
stays a clever argument.

20
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:10,748
And seeing them once is not enough.

21
00:01:10,828 --> 00:01:14,298
If we stop, the old
logic quietly comes back.

22
00:01:15,109 --> 00:01:21,088
The first. Every appearance is vivid, and
it cannot be found. Look at a red apple.

23
00:01:21,168 --> 00:01:25,015
The red is bright, impossible
to miss. Now look for it.

24
00:01:25,095 --> 00:01:28,099
Is it in the skin, in
the light, in the eye?

25
00:01:28,179 --> 00:01:31,686
It is not found in any of
them, and not anywhere else.

26
00:01:31,766 --> 00:01:35,246
Yet the apple is still
red, as vivid as before.

27
00:01:35,326 --> 00:01:37,909
Not vivid first and empty later.

28
00:01:37,989 --> 00:01:41,061
Not empty underneath and
vivid on the surface.

29
00:01:41,141 --> 00:01:46,265
Confirm only the vividness, and
presence turns into a new ground.

30
00:01:46,345 --> 00:01:52,067
Confirm only the unfindability,
and the world turns thin and void.

31
00:01:52,147 --> 00:01:55,463
Both have to be seen together,
in the same appearing.

32
00:01:55,543 --> 00:01:57,773
The tradition calls this emptiness.

33
00:01:57,853 --> 00:02:01,252
Not a void, and not a
ground behind the appearing.

34
00:02:01,332 --> 00:02:03,702
Only the appearing's not being found.

35
00:02:04,518 --> 00:02:09,058
The second. Appearance arises
whenever its conditions come together.

36
00:02:09,138 --> 00:02:14,343
Light, a surface, an eye,
attention: together, red appears.

37
00:02:14,423 --> 00:02:16,667
When one is missing, it does not.

38
00:02:16,747 --> 00:02:20,987
Nothing comes out of a hidden place,
and nothing goes back into one.

39
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:24,751
And the conditions are not a
solid network behind the display.

40
00:02:24,831 --> 00:02:27,251
They too are vivid, and not found.

41
00:02:27,331 --> 00:02:30,312
The tradition calls this
dependent origination.

42
00:02:31,138 --> 00:02:35,746
The third. We habitually and
intuitively think inherently,

43
00:02:35,826 --> 00:02:38,993
and the way we do it follows
the shape of our language.

44
00:02:39,073 --> 00:02:41,683
A sentence wants a subject and a verb.

45
00:02:41,763 --> 00:02:45,623
So we say "the wind blows",
and "lightning flashes",

46
00:02:45,704 --> 00:02:48,191
as if there were a wind
apart from the blowing,

47
00:02:48,271 --> 00:02:50,601
and a lightning apart from the flash.

48
00:02:50,731 --> 00:02:54,034
"I see the tree" puts a seer on one side,

49
00:02:54,114 --> 00:02:57,553
a tree on the other, and an
act of seeing between them.

50
00:02:57,633 --> 00:03:00,166
The grammar becomes the
picture of the world.

51
00:03:00,998 --> 00:03:03,092
But experience is never like that.

52
00:03:03,172 --> 00:03:05,130
The flashing is the lightning.

53
00:03:05,210 --> 00:03:06,856
The blowing is the wind.

54
00:03:06,936 --> 00:03:11,897
This does not mean a pure, wordless
world lies underneath the words.

55
00:03:11,977 --> 00:03:13,500
That would be one more floor.

56
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:17,793
It means only that the picture of things
standing behind what happens was never

57
00:03:17,873 --> 00:03:19,628
found in experience.

58
00:03:19,708 --> 00:03:22,195
And this habit runs almost by default.

59
00:03:22,275 --> 00:03:26,272
It bends every experience
and insight back into things,

60
00:03:26,352 --> 00:03:28,975
selves and grounds before we notice.

61
00:03:29,055 --> 00:03:32,155
So practice is not collecting experiences.

62
00:03:32,235 --> 00:03:35,728
It is undoing these
habits, again and again.

63
00:03:35,808 --> 00:03:38,024
The tradition calls this ignorance.

64
00:03:38,104 --> 00:03:43,024
Not a lack of information, but the innate
grasping at things as existing from their

65
00:03:43,104 --> 00:03:44,304
own side.

66
00:03:44,994 --> 00:03:47,183
The fourth. There is no given.

67
00:03:47,263 --> 00:03:51,531
No world is already there,
with its own edges and things,

68
00:03:51,611 --> 00:03:53,759
waiting behind what appears.

69
00:03:53,839 --> 00:03:58,488
One bowl of liquid is water
to us, pus to a hungry ghost,

70
00:03:58,568 --> 00:04:00,186
a home to a fish.

71
00:04:00,266 --> 00:04:03,379
The habit says a bowl of
something must sit underneath,

72
00:04:03,459 --> 00:04:06,721
a neutral stuff that each
being merely filters.

73
00:04:06,801 --> 00:04:09,058
Look for it, and it is not found.

74
00:04:09,138 --> 00:04:12,971
What appears, and how it is
picked out, arise together.

75
00:04:13,051 --> 00:04:16,939
Beings still agree, and the
world still holds together,

76
00:04:17,019 --> 00:04:19,208
with no hidden object beneath it.

77
00:04:19,288 --> 00:04:21,355
Nor is the mind the floor instead.

78
00:04:21,434 --> 00:04:25,612
Mind and object arise together,
and neither comes first.

79
00:04:26,446 --> 00:04:30,211
The first two are one
fact, seen from two sides.

80
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:35,605
Nāgārjuna says that what arises
dependently is what is called emptiness.

81
00:04:35,685 --> 00:04:37,915
The third is what hides that fact.

82
00:04:37,995 --> 00:04:40,972
The fourth takes away
its last hiding place:

83
00:04:41,052 --> 00:04:43,205
a given world beneath it all.

84
00:04:44,005 --> 00:04:45,840
Anatta is the first door.

85
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:50,637
In seeing, no seer is found:
no doer behind the doing.

86
00:04:50,717 --> 00:04:54,550
Nāgārjuna takes the same
insight through every thing:

87
00:04:54,630 --> 00:04:58,802
the walker, the fire, the
cause, even the seeing.

88
00:04:58,882 --> 00:05:01,058
And where do the four insights lead?

89
00:05:01,138 --> 00:05:04,658
When the habit stops, and
no given is left beneath,

90
00:05:04,738 --> 00:05:07,186
the first two are tasted together.

91
00:05:07,266 --> 00:05:11,126
With no doer anywhere, and
nothing put in its place,

92
00:05:11,206 --> 00:05:13,123
nothing is making the appearing.

93
00:05:13,203 --> 00:05:16,180
The sound is not a product
waiting to be finished.

94
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:21,384
It is already complete, by itself,
exactly as its conditions meet.

95
00:05:21,464 --> 00:05:24,984
The Dzogchen tradition calls
this spontaneous presence,

96
00:05:25,064 --> 00:05:27,240
the last of the seven phases.

97
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:30,474
Not uncaused, and not
a source behind things.

98
00:05:30,554 --> 00:05:34,160
Dependent arising itself,
met without the fixing.

99
00:05:34,998 --> 00:05:37,011
Why does the logic need the seeing?

100
00:05:37,091 --> 00:05:39,647
The two logics can be learned as ideas.

101
00:05:39,727 --> 00:05:42,867
One starts with things, and
asks what happens to them.

102
00:05:42,947 --> 00:05:46,291
The other asks how anything is
picked out as a thing at all.

103
00:05:46,371 --> 00:05:50,013
Explained like this, the difference
takes a minute to follow,

104
00:05:50,093 --> 00:05:51,920
and a minute to agree with.

105
00:05:52,738 --> 00:05:54,832
But agreeing changes very little.

106
00:05:54,912 --> 00:05:58,093
The logic of substance
is not a belief we hold.

107
00:05:58,173 --> 00:06:01,449
It is how things seem, before any thought:

108
00:06:01,529 --> 00:06:04,357
the cup is simply there, on its own side.

109
00:06:04,437 --> 00:06:08,668
Seen this way, even the new logic
is read through the old one.

110
00:06:08,771 --> 00:06:11,775
Things are still things;
now they also depend.

111
00:06:11,855 --> 00:06:14,452
The conditions become a new solid floor.

112
00:06:14,532 --> 00:06:20,457
Emptiness becomes a void, or a vast space
behind it all. The words have changed.

113
00:06:20,537 --> 00:06:21,956
The logic has not.

114
00:06:22,777 --> 00:06:24,246
So what is a phenomenon?

115
00:06:24,326 --> 00:06:29,123
A vivid appearing that is not found,
even while it is appearing vividly.

116
00:06:29,203 --> 00:06:31,515
Vivid: nothing is taken away.

117
00:06:31,595 --> 00:06:36,284
The red is red, a sound is heard,
and a car can still knock you down.

118
00:06:36,364 --> 00:06:40,183
Not found: not in its parts,
and not apart from them.

119
00:06:40,263 --> 00:06:43,811
Not out there, and not in
here as an image in the mind.

120
00:06:43,891 --> 00:06:46,379
And the mind that looks
is not found either.

121
00:06:46,459 --> 00:06:50,047
Not even "nowhere": the
absence is not a place,

122
00:06:50,127 --> 00:06:51,800
or a void left over.

123
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:56,392
Dependent already: the red is
dependent in the very moment it is red.

124
00:06:56,472 --> 00:06:59,110
And clear, with no knower behind it.

125
00:06:59,190 --> 00:07:02,221
The clarity belongs to
the appearing itself.

126
00:07:02,301 --> 00:07:04,708
It is not a light shining from a witness,

127
00:07:04,788 --> 00:07:06,474
and it is empty too.

128
00:07:06,554 --> 00:07:11,655
No phenomenon, not even the mind,
is the floor the others stand on.

129
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:17,449
Before any of this can work, one thing
has to be admitted. We think inherently.

130
00:07:17,529 --> 00:07:22,557
Not now and then, and not only when
we philosophise. It is our default.

131
00:07:22,637 --> 00:07:25,859
Seeing it means noticing,
in an ordinary day,

132
00:07:25,939 --> 00:07:29,962
that our thinking is still built
on things standing on their own:

133
00:07:30,042 --> 00:07:34,949
a self that decides, a world out
there, a problem that is simply there.

134
00:07:35,029 --> 00:07:36,919
It does not feel like a view at all.

135
00:07:36,999 --> 00:07:38,757
It feels like how things are.

136
00:07:39,561 --> 00:07:45,214
If this is not seen, even deep experience
and genuine insight will hit a wall.

137
00:07:45,294 --> 00:07:49,345
The experience can be non
dual, and the insight true,

138
00:07:49,425 --> 00:07:52,701
while the framework that
reads them is still inherent.

139
00:07:52,781 --> 00:07:57,103
Then presence becomes a ground,
emptiness becomes a void,

140
00:07:57,183 --> 00:08:00,459
and conditions become
things causing things.

141
00:08:00,539 --> 00:08:04,037
The experience has changed.
The framework has not.

142
00:08:04,837 --> 00:08:09,607
Many practitioners, especially in Zen,
hold that direct experience is what

143
00:08:09,687 --> 00:08:13,086
matters, and that view
and logic come second.

144
00:08:13,166 --> 00:08:15,726
The author calls this a grave mistake.

145
00:08:15,829 --> 00:08:21,265
From that starting point, practice becomes
the removal of concepts. Not thinking.

146
00:08:21,345 --> 00:08:23,742
Bare attention. Naked awareness.

147
00:08:24,558 --> 00:08:27,087
These practices do something genuine.

148
00:08:27,167 --> 00:08:32,046
With the commentary quiet, the luminous
clarity of appearances can be tasted

149
00:08:32,126 --> 00:08:37,875
directly: sounds, colours and
sensations shining by themselves.

150
00:08:37,955 --> 00:08:40,090
But at most, that is all they do.

151
00:08:40,170 --> 00:08:43,446
Removing concepts does not
show what appearances are.

152
00:08:43,526 --> 00:08:48,269
Tasted vividly, they can still be
taken as existing from their own side.

153
00:08:48,349 --> 00:08:52,726
The mind can be tasted too,
as pure, clear awareness,

154
00:08:52,806 --> 00:08:56,448
and then taken as the one
thing that stands by itself.

155
00:08:56,528 --> 00:08:59,410
But the mind is a
phenomenon like any other.

156
00:08:59,490 --> 00:09:03,151
Its clarity is as empty
as the red of the apple.

157
00:09:03,957 --> 00:09:08,931
Even the idea behind these practices
pictures concepts as labels over a given

158
00:09:09,011 --> 00:09:11,282
world, to be peeled off.

159
00:09:11,362 --> 00:09:14,502
That picture is itself
the logic of substance.

160
00:09:14,582 --> 00:09:17,627
A thing and its
designation arise together.

161
00:09:17,707 --> 00:09:20,983
There is no unlabelled layer
waiting to be uncovered.

162
00:09:21,063 --> 00:09:25,249
Strip the labels, and the habit
stays, now without comment.

163
00:09:25,329 --> 00:09:28,265
That is how luminous
clarity becomes a Witness,

164
00:09:28,345 --> 00:09:30,494
a ground, a Source.

165
00:09:30,574 --> 00:09:33,718
It was the author's own
story in the I AM years.

166
00:09:34,550 --> 00:09:37,853
Bare attention can taste
the clarity of appearances.

167
00:09:37,933 --> 00:09:39,950
Only the view shows what they are.

168
00:09:40,770 --> 00:09:44,141
The great masters said the
same, in their own ways.

169
00:09:44,221 --> 00:09:49,943
Atiśa wrote that calm abiding alone,
without the wisdom that sees emptiness,

170
00:09:50,023 --> 00:09:52,307
does not end the obstructions.

171
00:09:52,387 --> 00:09:56,207
Rongzom traced the habit
behind appearances to a view:

172
00:09:56,287 --> 00:09:58,503
the view of real entities.

173
00:09:58,583 --> 00:10:04,060
Dōgen, a Zen master, scolded those in his
day who thought the old Zen stories were

174
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:06,044
beyond logical thought.

175
00:10:06,124 --> 00:10:08,965
Longchenpa advised that
when thoughts arise,

176
00:10:09,045 --> 00:10:11,220
the direct view is crucial.

177
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:16,089
Tsongkhapa wrote that without the
wisdom that realises how things are,

178
00:10:16,219 --> 00:10:21,166
even renunciation and compassion
cannot cut existence at its root.

179
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:27,189
And Mipham taught that, just as the "I" is
a conceptual label, so are all phenomena.

180
00:10:27,993 --> 00:10:30,589
None of them says
experience does not matter.

181
00:10:30,669 --> 00:10:35,168
Hearing that there is water does not
quench thirst; only drinking does.

182
00:10:35,248 --> 00:10:38,325
But experience without the
view cannot do the work.

183
00:10:39,173 --> 00:10:43,632
For the author, after I AM, the
vividness was never what was missing.

184
00:10:43,712 --> 00:10:46,716
What was missing was seeing
what that vividness is.

185
00:10:46,796 --> 00:10:50,507
What changed things was seeing
directly what a phenomenon is:

186
00:10:50,587 --> 00:10:54,324
vivid and nowhere, with no
knower behind the knowing,

187
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:56,757
and no ground behind the appearing.

188
00:10:56,837 --> 00:11:00,153
Only then did the logic of
dependency become clear,

189
00:11:00,233 --> 00:11:03,011
not as a theory, but as how things are.

190
00:11:03,809 --> 00:11:05,468
Now return to the koan.

191
00:11:05,548 --> 00:11:07,981
This moment ceases as it arises.

192
00:11:08,061 --> 00:11:10,690
Does it arise, or does it cease?

193
00:11:11,493 --> 00:11:15,271
The logic of substance starts
with a thing: this moment.

194
00:11:15,351 --> 00:11:19,814
Arising and ceasing are what
happen to it. So it must choose.

195
00:11:20,617 --> 00:11:22,901
It arises? Then it is there.

196
00:11:22,981 --> 00:11:28,485
But it ceases as it arises, so it is
never there to have arisen. It ceases?

197
00:11:28,565 --> 00:11:30,265
Then something passes away.

198
00:11:30,345 --> 00:11:33,988
But what passes away,
if it never stood? Both?

199
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:37,616
Coming into being and
passing away are opposites.

200
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:41,230
They cannot belong to one
thing at one time. Neither?

201
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:42,901
Then nothing happens at all.

202
00:11:42,981 --> 00:11:45,242
Yet a sound is being heard right now.

203
00:11:46,061 --> 00:11:50,858
Every answer fails. Nāgārjuna
put the whole trap in one verse.

204
00:11:50,938 --> 00:11:56,379
There is no passing away either apart from
coming into being, or together with it.

205
00:11:57,190 --> 00:12:00,086
The logic of substance
looks for a way out:

206
00:12:00,166 --> 00:12:04,515
a timeless Now, an awareness
in which moments come and go.

207
00:12:04,595 --> 00:12:09,017
Each keeps the moment as a thing,
and only moves it somewhere else.

208
00:12:09,829 --> 00:12:13,186
The logic of dependency
starts one step earlier.

209
00:12:13,266 --> 00:12:16,067
It asks how "this moment"
is picked out at all.

210
00:12:16,147 --> 00:12:20,075
A moment is picked out together
with its arising and its ceasing.

211
00:12:20,155 --> 00:12:24,001
None comes first, and none is
found apart from the others.

212
00:12:24,081 --> 00:12:28,417
In the author's words: the
moment doesn't arise nor cease,

213
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:32,104
but is merely designated
as such upon conditions.

214
00:12:32,961 --> 00:12:35,558
Think of a staircase. Up, or down?

215
00:12:35,638 --> 00:12:39,131
In themselves, neither:
up for someone climbing,

216
00:12:39,211 --> 00:12:41,020
down for someone coming down.

217
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:44,240
And they are truly climbed.
The moment is the same.

218
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:47,614
It is not nothing, and it
is not only in the mind.

219
00:12:48,429 --> 00:12:53,430
So "ceases as it arises" is not a
paradox. It is a plain description.

220
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:59,042
There is no "it" standing between the
arising and the ceasing, to do either.

221
00:12:59,122 --> 00:13:02,103
The question is not
answered. It falls away.

222
00:13:02,918 --> 00:13:06,982
The eight steps of The Logic each
come back to this from one side.

223
00:13:07,062 --> 00:13:12,322
What exactly is denied: only the
"it", the moment standing on its own.

224
00:13:12,402 --> 00:13:16,697
Looked for, like the old masters'
chariot, it is not found.

225
00:13:16,777 --> 00:13:19,740
Yet moments are named, counted and timed.

226
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:23,219
Conventionally, the
train leaves and arrives.

227
00:13:23,299 --> 00:13:25,352
One moment, met two ways.

228
00:13:25,432 --> 00:13:29,238
And it is because nothing stands
on its own that things can arise,

229
00:13:29,318 --> 00:13:34,265
change and work. The last step
gathers it all into four questions.

230
00:13:34,345 --> 00:13:36,058
What would a substance view say?

231
00:13:36,138 --> 00:13:38,205
What does dependency say instead?

232
00:13:38,285 --> 00:13:41,538
What is affirmed conventionally?
What is never found?

233
00:13:42,354 --> 00:13:45,046
The same logic reaches beyond the moment.

234
00:13:45,126 --> 00:13:49,951
Look for the one who changed, apart
from the changing, and none is found.

235
00:13:50,031 --> 00:13:52,600
Yet a promise I made
is still mine to keep.

236
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:55,318
Close your hand, and a fist appears.

237
00:13:55,398 --> 00:13:58,810
Open it, and the fist is
gone. It went nowhere.

238
00:13:58,890 --> 00:14:03,293
Look for a friend apart from the face,
the voice and the years of meeting,

239
00:14:03,373 --> 00:14:09,373
and no one is found. Yet when they die,
someone lived, was loved, and is missed.

240
00:14:10,401 --> 00:14:13,459
Nothing is lost when
the "it" is not found.

241
00:14:13,539 --> 00:14:15,117
The sound is still heard.

242
00:14:15,197 --> 00:14:17,019
Actions still bear fruit.

243
00:14:17,099 --> 00:14:22,359
Dependent arising is not a lesser layer
over something that stands by itself.

244
00:14:22,439 --> 00:14:24,782
There is nothing
underneath for it to cover.

245
00:14:25,597 --> 00:14:27,392
So, a few things to try.

246
00:14:27,472 --> 00:14:29,865
Listen to one sound until it ends.

247
00:14:29,945 --> 00:14:32,990
Notice how vivid it was.
Then ask where it was.

248
00:14:33,070 --> 00:14:35,462
Don't answer with a thought; just look.

249
00:14:35,542 --> 00:14:37,215
Look at a colour in front of you.

250
00:14:37,295 --> 00:14:41,386
Is there a seer behind the seeing,
apart from the colour being seen?

251
00:14:41,466 --> 00:14:44,090
Say to yourself, "the wind is blowing".

252
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:46,115
Then feel the wind on your skin.

253
00:14:46,195 --> 00:14:48,320
Is there a wind apart from the blowing?

254
00:14:49,121 --> 00:14:54,575
Listen to a sound once more. It is vivid.
It is gone. And nothing went anywhere.

255
00:14:55,389 --> 00:14:58,855
Ask what arises, and
the koan is a paradox.

256
00:14:58,935 --> 00:15:03,887
See that no "it" is found, and
the koan is simply this moment.

